splitcode
------------------------------------------
splitcode is a tool that enables flexible and efficient preprocessing, parsing,
and manipulation of sequencing reads according to a user’s specifications.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libhts3-1.25-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libz-ng2-2.3.3-1bl2

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libhts-devel-1.25-1bl1
  libz-ng-devel-2.3.3-1bl2
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/pachterlab/splitcode

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/pachterlab/splitcode/archive/refs/tags/v0.31.6.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack splitcode-0.31.6-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./splitcode-0.31.6-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/splitcode-0.31.6-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/splitcode-0.31.6-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(splitcode)
  /usr/bin/splitcode.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/splitcode.README
  /usr/share/doc/splitcode/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/splitcode/README.md

